      "title": "Mandates and essential health benefits",
      "text": "Maryland’s benchmark plan for essential health benefits incorporates the state mandates that existed when the benchmark was chosen, so individual and small group plans carry them as essential benefits. Mandates added later may require the state to defray the added premium cost in subsidized plans, which is why the Health Care Commission reviews each proposal.",
